  "question": {
    "text": "A metal complex with a formula $\\mathrm{MC} \\ell_4 \\cdot 3 \\mathrm{NH}_3$ is involved in $\\mathrm{sp}^3 \\mathrm{~d}^2$ hybridisation. It upon reaction with excess of $\\mathrm{AgNO}_3$ solution gives ' x ' moles of AgCl. Consider ' x ' is equal to the number of lone pairs of electron present in central atom of $\\mathrm{BrF}_5$. Then the number of geometrical isomers exhibited by the complex is ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/n3uLzf4VxZX5d61GLqhzHlMvl7s-c8IJMQZqRq9bBrE.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/> 1 lone pair hence 1 mole AgCl.<br />Complex is $\\left[\\mathrm{M}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_3 \\mathrm{Cl}_3\\right] \\mathrm{Cl}$.<br />It shows 2 geometrical isomers $\\left(\\mathrm{Ma}_3 \\mathrm{~b}_3\\right.$ type) facial (fac) & meridional (Mer)",
    "image": null
  },
